+<p><strong>Pass:</strong> one qualified group pays the baseline and completes a witnessed safe-control rehearsal. It must then make one binding commitment at the stated €20,000 onboarding and €4,500 monthly retail hurdles: a production order, a non-refundable onboarding deposit, or a paid first month. A letter of interest or dated authority does not count. Written allocation and liability terms must accompany the commitment. <strong>Kill or downgrade:</strong> no paid baseline after five qualified offers; no eligible blocked investment; installer capture of all evidence and reusable work; or a paid baseline without a production commitment by day 90. The last outcome kills the recurring-company thesis and downgrades the offer to occasional integration consulting, if premium self-employment is acceptable.</p>
